{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "a1b2c3d4-e5f6-4789-aaaa-forgeshiftmig1",
    "name": "Forgeshift WSO2 → Kong Konnect Migration Service",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "description": "# WSO2 → Kong Konnect Migration Service\n\nMigrate WSO2 API Manager resources to Kong Konnect (via decK).\n\n## Quick start\n1. Set the collection **Variables** (tab above): `baseUrl`, `companyName`, `wso2Tenant`, `kongCtrlPlanId`, `kongRegion`.\n2. Get the WSO2 **sourceIds** you want to migrate from the discovery service:\n   `GET {discovery}/wso2/history/details?companyName=..&wso2Tenant=..&resourceType=apis` → copy an `id` into `apiSourceId`.\n3. Pick a request below and **Send**.\n\n## Folders\n- **1 · Single-resource migration (sync)** — migrate one type (apis / subscriptions / …). Blocks and returns the report.\n- **2 · Single-resource + auto-migrate dependencies** — same, but also pulls in dependencies and skips anything already in Kong.\n- **3 · Async + poll** — fire-and-forget + how to follow up.\n- **4 · Bulk migration** — migrate everything (or by type) from a discovery snapshot.\n- **5 · Track a job** — status, report, list, delete.\n\n## Sync vs async (every POST supports both)\n- **Sync** (default): blocks, returns `200` with `{ job, report }`.\n- **Async** (`?async=true`): returns `201` with a PENDING job → poll `GET /migrations/{id}` then `GET /migrations/{id}/report`.\n\n## The report (`GET /migrations/{id}/report`)\n`outcomes[]` (counts per type) · `apiKongDetails[]` (Kong service/routes/plugins per API) · `warnings[]` (errors + `SKIPPED_ALREADY_IN_KONG`) · `dependencyMigrations[]` (the resource + its dependencies, by name) · `deckApplyErrors` (real Kong apply result, from the pipeline callback)."
  },
