    {
      "name": "2 · Single-resource + auto-migrate dependencies",
      "description": "Set `includeDependencies: true` + `assessmentTransactionId` (the assessment run whose dependency graph to use).\n\nThe service auto-pulls each resource's dependencies (API → its subscriptions + consuming apps + products; product → its member APIs; etc.), **skips anything already in Kong** (Kong-authoritative), builds the YAML for the rest, and decK applies it.\n\nThe report's **`dependencyMigrations[]`** shows the resource + every dependency **by name**, each with an `alreadyInKong` flag; skipped ones also appear in `warnings[]` as `SKIPPED_ALREADY_IN_KONG`.\n\n> `assessmentTransactionId` = the `requestTransactionId` of an assessment run (`GET {assessment}/wso2/assessment/history?...`).",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Migrate API + its dependencies",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"companyName\": \"{{companyName}}\",\n  \"wso2Tenant\": \"{{wso2Tenant}}\",\n  \"userEmail\": \"{{userEmail}}\",\n  \"requestSource\": \"{{requestSource}}\",\n  \"requestTransactionId\": \"{{txnId}}\",\n  \"kongCtrlPlanId\": \"{{kongCtrlPlanId}}\",\n  \"kongRegion\": \"{{kongRegion}}\",\n  \"apis\": [\n    \"{{apiSourceId}}\"\n  ],\n  \"includeDependencies\": true,\n  \"assessmentTransactionId\": \"{{assessmentTransactionId}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/konnect/wso2/apis",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "konnect",
                "wso2",
                "apis"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Migrate one API **and** its subscriptions, consuming apps, and products — skipping whatever is already in Kong."
          },
          "response": []
        },
